-- title:
--   Automorphisms fixing j and j(qᵖ) stabilise both branch valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbf{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbf{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbf{Q}$ inside $\mathbf{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$. Let $j \in K$ have $q$-expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (the modular invariant, $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ`), with $j \ne 0$ assumed as an instance, and let $jp \in K$ have $q$-expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ p ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25), the series obtained from $j$ by multiplying all exponents by $p$. Let $W_0, W_1$ be valuation subrings of $K$ such that: (h1) each contains the image of $A$ and sends the maximal ideal of $A$ into its non-units; (h2) for each $i$ and each polynomial $P \in A[X]$ with non-zero reduction modulo the maximal ideal, both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $W_i$; (h3) $W_0 \ne W_1$; (h4) $W_0$ consists exactly of those $f \in K$ for which there are power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $\bar y \ne 0$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ after mapping coefficients to $L$; (h5) every valuation subring of $K$ with properties (h1) and (h2) equals $W_0$ or $W_1$. Then for every $L$-algebra automorphism $g$ of $K$ with $g(j) = j$ and $g(jp) = jp$, the preimages satisfy $g^{-1}(W_0) = W_0$ and $g^{-1}(W_1) = W_1$.
--
--   The two valuation subrings $W_0, W_1$ play the role of the two branches (Igusa components) of the special fibre at $p$ of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$, $W_0$ being the Gauss ring attached to the $q$-expansion; the statement says that any automorphism fixing both $j$ and $j(q^p)$ — in particular the diamond operators $\langle d \rangle$ — stabilises each branch rather than interchanging them. It is used in the analysis of minimal primes over the relevant span inside the chart algebra of $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_comap_eq_of_map_j_eq_of_map_jp_eq_valuationSubring_pair_x1_mul.lean

